$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Birch Reduction; Typical Procedure: The
aromatic compound (13.5 mmol) in MeOH (5 mL) was added to NH3 (45 mL)
condensed at -80°C. Small pieces of sodium (78 mmol, 1.8 g) were then
added. Once the sodium had disappeared (after a few minutes), Et2O (100
mL) and water (100 mL) were added. NH3 was cautiously removed under
vacuum. The aqueous layer was then extracted with Et2O. The organic
layers were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated under vacuum. The
crude material generally contained more than 95% of the desired product.
Purifications were performed by rapid silica gel chromatography under N2
using a mixture of pentane and Et2O in the appropriate ratio as eluent.
The final products were stored under argon at -20°C.
3-(4,7-Dihydrobenzo[1,3]dioxol-5-yl)propan-1-ol (2h), yield 35%. 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ = 1.3-1.5 (s, 1H, OH), 1.7 (tt, 2H, J = 8 Hz, J = 6.5 Hz,
CCH2C), 2.2 (t, 2H, J = 8 Hz, CCH2C=), 2.9 (s, 4H, 2 x CH2C=), 3.7 (t, J
= 6.5 Hz, 2H, CCH2O), 5.4-5.5 (m, 1H, CH=), 5.6 (s, 2H, OCH2O). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ = 24.2, 26.9, 30.6, 33.3, 62.3, 98.0, 117.6, 131.2, 134.2. IR
(neat): ν = 3364, 1769, 1720, 1444, 1409, 1327, 1206, 1034, 910 cm-1. MS
(DCI/NH3): m/z = 183 (MH)+, 200 (MNH4)+. Anal. Calcd for C10H14O3
(182.2): C, 65.92; H, 7.74; Found: C, 66.03; H, 7.83.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reinvestigation of Birch reduction of benzo[1,3]dioxoles and further
transformations of the resulting dihydro compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sylvain, Catherine; Wagner, Alain; Mioskowski, Charles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1998), (7), 970-972

