1.36 (m, 1H), 1.40-1.49 (m, 1H), 1.63-1.69 (m, 2H), 1.94 (s, 3H),
2.11-2.24 (m, 2H), 2.65-2.78 (m, 2H), 3.02-3.15 (m, 4H), 3.18- 3.30 (m,
1H), 4.26-4.33 (m, 1H), 5.55-5.59 (m, 1H), 5.76-5.83 (m, 2H); 13C NMR
(126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.0 (d, JP,C = 2.7 Hz), 15.7, 21.2, 22.1, 22.8, 23.7,
25.7, 27.4 (d, JP,C = 6.4 Hz), 31.5, 34.2, 38.9 (d, JP,C = 3.6 Hz), 43.2,
44.7 (d, JP,C = 128.1 Hz), 49.0 (d, JP,C = 5.5 Hz), 75.5 (d, JP,C = 8.2
Hz), 122.0 (d, JP,C = 11.8 Hz), 123.3 (d, JP,C = 10.0 Hz), 126.0 (d, JP,C
= 10.9 Hz), 129.5 (d, JP,C = 8.2 Hz); 31P NMR (202 MHz, CDCl3) δ 25.76;
GC tR = 13.51 min; GC-MS (EI, 70 eV) m/z = 367 (M+) (0.1), 139 (23), 138
(48), 137 (19), 136 (14), 122 (22), 97 (15), 95 (20), 93 (15), 92 (15),
91 (27), 83 (100), 81 (24); C21H38NO2P (367.26): calcd C 68.63, H 10.42,
N 3.81; found C 68.59, H 10.19, N 3.62. Minor Diastereomer. Rf = 0.78
(CHCl3/MeOH = 15:1); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.70 (d, JH,H = 6.6 Hz,
3H), 0.82 (d, JH,H = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 0.87 (d, JH,H = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 0.83-0.93
(m, 2H), 0.97 (t, JH,H = 7.1 Hz, 6H), 1.22 (q, JH,H = 11.4 Hz, 1H),
